{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The components are those of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":" without the trivial ones, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Empty exactly when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attractingComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":", so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices do not start at 0."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so one sort by that vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position puts the components in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", where positions are insertion order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(V + E)."}]}],"name":"Complexity"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through both."}],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","role":"collection","title":"Connectivity"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"type":"topic","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","title":"DirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"symbol"}}}